88
3° there are linked offences in a way that one
of them was the cause of another;
4° a person keeps for the offender items
which have a connection with the offence.
Indivisibility of offences occurs when:
1° a single offence is committed by several
persons;
2° one person commits several offences with
the same intent;
3° one person commits several offences in a
way that one of them constitutes the
aggravating circumstance of the other.

